# Security Rules

## Secrets

- Never hardcode keys/tokens/passwords
- No dummy Claude/Anthropic keys on production paths
- Never log API keys or key prefixes
- Document new secrets in `docs/ENVIRONMENT.md` + `.env.example`

## Auth

- ECDSA headers required in non-dev
- Dev bypass only when `NODE_ENV=development` AND `x-dev-mode: true`
- Bypass must not work when `NODE_ENV=production`

## Logging

- Nest: bunyan only
- Lambda: structured + redacted; no full event payload dumps

## AWS

- Least-privilege IAM; justify any `*` resources
- Prefer RDS CA verification; document temporary `rejectUnauthorized: false`
- Prefer OIDC for GitHub→AWS (SHOULD, non-blocking)
